Description: USB sticks load themselves, and the sidebar never shows the Mixxx tree
 1. A rekordbox stick is browsed the moment it is plugged in. LibraryControl
    polls /media/USBA and /media/USBB once a second; a slot that newly holds a
    mounted filesystem with PIONEER/rekordbox/export.pdb is browsed exactly as
    if its USB button had been pressed (a stick already in at boot is picked
    up on the first tick after the skin exists). A slot that stops being
    mounted -- pulled without an eject -- triggers a device rescan, so its row
    and the sidebar rooted at it go away instead of lingering. A new stick
    waits while a USB hold or eject is running, and when both sticks appear
    in the same tick only the first is opened.
 .
 2. The playlists of a freshly parsed stick now appear without another press.
    parseDeviceDB() attaches them to the device's TreeItem on the worker
    thread with no model notifications, so the sidebar -- rooted at the
    device while it was still empty -- kept showing an empty list. The only
    way out was to press the button twice more: once to un-root (showing the
    whole stock Mixxx tree) and once to root again. RekordboxFeature now
    emits devicePlaylistsReady() when a parse lands, and LibraryControl
    re-applies the root, which makes the view lay out again.
 .
 3. The stock Mixxx tree (Tracks, Auto DJ, Playlists, Crates, Computer,
    Recordings, History, Analyze...) is never shown. With no stick open, the
    sidebar is rooted at the Rekordbox feature, i.e. just the list of sticks
    that are in (empty when there are none). A press on the stick that is
    already open no longer un-roots it; it goes back to the top of the stick,
    like a CDJ's source button. A model reset, which drops a view's root,
    puts the stick list back.
 .
 4. Device rescans started by LibraryControl are silent. They used to go
    through the feature's activate() -- what a tap on "Rekordbox" in the full
    tree does -- which also switched the library pane to the Rekordbox help
    page and selected the feature in the sidebar. RekordboxFeature::
    rescanDevices() scans without either, and queues a request that arrives
    mid-scan rather than dropping it (the running scan may have read /media
    before the new mount). A tap-driven activate() is unchanged.
 .
 Skin side: none.
Author: Pioneered fork
Forwarded: no

